   1108  fd39							; block lives with the walk where there is hole).
   1109  fd39							; --- Phase 3: phase-cell blink (PF buffer pokes) ----------------------
   1110  fd39							; Body moved after the level data (PhaseBlink, ~130B — the StageBandTab
   1111  fd39							; window $F3C4..$F4C4 was full; the data window has the only free
   1112  fd39							; hole). Contract: clobbers A/X/Y/FetchPtr/RectCount/LineCount/
   1113  fd39							; CollisionCellX/CollisionEndY ($8F scratch — the pack below rebuilds
   1114  fd39							; it). The PF buffers ARE the collision map (cell walk + laser read
   1115  fd39							; them) — toggling the cell's two bits THERE makes render + PHM +
   1116  fd39							; laser follow with zero kernel cost. 64f full cycle = EnemyRamP bit5
   1117  fd39							; (32 on + 32 off; clock-derived, no state bytes — locked plan).
   1118  fd39							; --- PhaseBlink ping-pong (chunk A2): it MUST run after the band/ball
   1119  fd39							; staging above and before the pack below (the crunch walk overwrites
   1120  fd39							; Temp/BandTab for its cell — running it earlier let SBT's own staging
   1121  fd39							; erase the crunch mask, and every crunch kill stopped latching).
   1122  fd39							; Leg 1: this `sta` runs here, the fetch at $F803 is bank2's
   1123  fd39							; `jmp PhBlinkTail` (byte-image pinned in bank2.asm).
